            </div>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="landing-section">
        <div class="landing-container" style="max-width: 860px;">
            <h1 class="mb-2">Terms of Service</h1>
            <p class="text-muted mb-5">Last updated: July 21, 2026</p>

            <h4>1. Acceptance of terms</h4>
            <p>
                By registering a company workspace or signing in to HrmSystem, you agree to these
                Terms of Service and to the <a href="privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you use the
                platform on behalf of a company, you confirm you are authorized to bind that company
                to these terms.
            </p>

            <h4 class="mt-4">2. The service</h4>
            <p>
                HrmSystem provides each registered company with an isolated HR workspace covering
                employee management, departments, attendance tracking, leave requests, analytics,
                announcements, data import/export, and team chat. Features available to you depend
                on the role assigned to your account (Tenant Admin, Manager, or Employee).
            </p>

            <h4 class="mt-4">3. Accounts and responsibilities</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>The person who registers a workspace becomes its founding Tenant Admin and is responsible for the accounts they provision inside it.</li>
                <li>You must keep your credentials confidential and notify your workspace administrator of any suspected unauthorized access.</li>
                <li>Workspace administrators are responsible for the accuracy and lawfulness of the employee data they enter or import, including having a legal basis to process their employees' personal data.</li>
            </ul>

            <h4 class="mt-4">4. Acceptable use</h4>
            <p>You agree not to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Attempt to access data belonging to another company's workspace.</li>
                <li>Probe, scan, overload, or otherwise interfere with the service (authentication endpoints are rate-limited and abuse may lead to suspension).</li>
                <li>Upload malicious files or content that is unlawful, harassing, or infringes the rights of others — including in chat messages and announcements.</li>
                <li>Use the service to store data you have no right to process.</li>
            </ul>

            <h4 class="mt-4">5. Your data</h4>
            <p>
                Your company owns the data in its workspace. Administrators can export it at any time
                in JSON, CSV, or XML. The platform takes automated daily backups solely for disaster
                recovery. Handling of personal data is described in the
                <a href="privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
            </p>

            <h4 class="mt-4">6. Availability</h4>
            <p>
                We aim for high availability and publish live component health on the public
                <a href="status">status page</a>, but the service is provided "as is" without a
                guaranteed service level. Planned maintenance and incidents are reflected there.
            </p>

            <h4 class="mt-4">7. Suspension and termination</h4>
            <p>
                Workspace administrators may suspend or reinstate accounts inside their workspace.
                The platform operator may suspend accounts or workspaces that materially breach these
                terms, with notice where practical. Upon workspace termination, its data is removed
                after the backup retention window elapses.
            </p>

            <h4 class="mt-4">8. Liability</h4>
            <p>
                To the maximum extent permitted by law, the platform operator is not liable for
                indirect or consequential damages, loss of profits, or loss of data resulting from
                use of the service. Nothing in these terms excludes liability that cannot legally be
                excluded.
            </p>

            <h4 class="mt-4">9. Changes to these terms</h4>
            <p>
                We may update these terms as the service evolves. Material changes will be announced
                inside the application; continued use after a change constitutes acceptance.
            </p>

            <h4 class="mt-4">10. Contact</h4>
            <p>
                Questions about these terms: <strong>legal@hrmsystem.example</strong>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="landing-footer">
        <div class="landing-container landing-footer-inner">
